WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.982
The word pretrained covers several very different practical categories.

00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:13.332
A base checkpoint has learned general language patterns and is often a starting point for feature extraction

00:00:13.332 --> 00:00:15.932
or later fine-tuning.

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:22.352
A task-fine-tuned checkpoint has already been adapted for a specific objective such as sentiment,

00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:27.707
named entity recognition, question answering, or summarization.

00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:33.747
An instruction or chat model has been post-trained to respond to natural-language instructions and

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:35.322
conversation formats.

00:00:35.322 --> 00:00:42.467
An embedding model is optimized to place semantically related texts near one another in vector space.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:50.692
A reranker, often a cross-encoder, scores a query and candidate text together to improve search ordering.

00:00:50.692 --> 00:00:57.302
Domain models are pretrained or adapted on specialized language such as biomedical, legal, financial,

00:00:57.302 --> 00:01:01.582
or scientific text. These categories can overlap.

00:01:01.582 --> 00:01:06.912
For example, a biomedical model may also be task-fine-tuned.

00:01:06.912 --> 00:01:11.838
Always inspect what training and objective produced the exact checkpoint.
